{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-luk-14-1","title":"Luke 14:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ heals the dropsy on the sabbath; 7 teaches humility; 12 to feast the poor; 15 under the parable of the great supper, shows how worldly minded men, who contemn the word of God, shall be shut out of heaven. 25 Those who will be his disciples, to bear their cross must make their accounts beforehand, lest with shame they revolt from him afterward; 34 and become altogether unprofitable, like salt that has lost its savour.</p>\n<p>as. 7:34-36; 11:37; 1Co 9:19-22 chief. Joh 3:1; Ac 5:34 they. 6:7; 11:53,54; 20:20; Ps 37:32; 41:6; 62:4; 64:5,6; Pr 23:7; Isa 29:20 Isa 29:21; Jer 20:10,11; Mr 3:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-3","title":"Luke 14:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the lawyers. 11:44,45 Is. 6:9; 13:14-16; Mt 12:10; Mr 3:4; Joh 7:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-4","title":"Luke 14:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Mt 21:25-27; 22:46</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-5","title":"Luke 14:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Which. 13:15; Ex 23:4,5; Da 4:24; Mt 12:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-6","title":"Luke 14:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>13:17; 20:26,40; 21:15; Ac 6:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-7","title":"Luke 14:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>put. Jud 14:12; Pr 8:1; Eze 17:2; Mt 13:34 they. 11:43; 20:46; Mt 23:6; Mr 12:38,39; Ac 8:18,19; Php 2:3; 3Jo 1:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-8","title":"Luke 14:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>When.That there were among the Jews of these times many disputes about seats at banquets, we learn both from Josephus and the Rabbis; nor were these matters unattended to by the Greeks and Romans. Similar admonitions to this of our Lord, also occur in the Rabbinical writers. Rabbi Akiba said, Go two or three seats lower than the place that belongs to thee, and sit there till they say unto to thee, Go up higher; but do not take the uppermost seat, lest they say unto thee, Come down: for it is better they should say unto thee, Go up, go up than they should say, Go down, go down.</p>\n<p>Pr 25:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-9","title":"Luke 14:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>and thou. Es 6:6-12; Pr 3:35; 11:2; 16:18; Eze 28:2-10; Da 4:30-34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-10","title":"Luke 14:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>go. 1Sa 15:17; Pr 15:33; 25:6,7 then. Isa 60:14; Re 3:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-11","title":"Luke 14:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>whosoever. 1:51; 18:14; 1Sa 15:17; Job 22:29; 40:10-12; Ps 18:27; 138:6 Pr 15:33; 18:12; 29:23; Isa 2:11,17; 57:15; Mt 23:12; Jas 4:6 1Pe 5:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-12","title":"Luke 14:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>when. 1:53; Pr 14:20; 22:16; Jas 2:1-6 and a. 6:32-36; Zec 7:5-7; Mt 5:46; 6:1-4,16-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-13","title":"Luke 14:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>call. 21; 11:41; De 14:29; 16:11,14; 26:12,13; 2Sa 6:19; 2Ch 30:24 Ne 8:10,12; Job 29:13,15,16; 31:16-20; Pr 3:9,10; 14:31; 31:6,7 Isa 58:7,10; Mt 14:14-21; 15:32-39; 22:10; Ac 2:44,45; 4:34,35; 9:39 Ro 12:13-16; 1Ti 3:2; 5:10; Tit 1:8; Phm 1:7; Heb 13:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-14","title":"Luke 14:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>for thou. Pr 19:17; Mt 6:4; 10:41,42; 25:34-40; Php 4:18,19 the resurrection. 20:35,36; Da 12:2,3; Joh 5:29; Ac 24:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-15","title":"Luke 14:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Blessed. 12:37; 13:29; 22:30; Mt 8:11; 25:10; Joh 6:27-59; Re 19:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-16","title":"Luke 14:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>A certain. Pr 9:1,2; Isa 25:6,7; Jer 31:12-14; Zec 10:7; Mt 22:2-14 bade. So 5:1; Isa 55:1-7; Mr 16:15,16; Re 3:20; 22:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-17","title":"Luke 14:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>his. 3:4-6; 9:1-5; 10:1-12; Pr 9:1-5; Mt 3:1-12; 10:1-4; Ac 2:38,39 Ac 3:24-26; 13:26,38,39 Come. Mt 11:27-29; 22:3,4; Joh 7:37; 2Co 5:18-21; 6:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-18","title":"Luke 14:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>all. 20:4,5; Isa 28:12,13; 29:11,12; Jer 5:4,5; 6:10,16,17; Mt 22:5,6 Joh 1:11; 5:40; Ac 13:45,46; 18:5,6; 28:25-27 I have. 8:14; 17:26-31; 18:24; Mt 24:38,39; 1Ti 6:9,10; 2Ti 4:4,10 Heb 12:16; 1Jo 2:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-20","title":"Luke 14:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>26-28; 18:29,30; 1Co 7:29-31,33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-21","title":"Luke 14:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>and shewed. 9:10; 1Sa 25:12; Mt 15:12; 18:31; Heb 13:17 being. 24; Ps 2:12; Mt 22:7,8; Heb 2:3; 12:25,26; Re 15:1-8; 19:15 Go. 24:47; Pr 1:20-25; 8:2-4; 9:3-4; Jer 5:1; Zec 11:7,11; Mt 21:28-31 Joh 4:39-42; 7:47-49; 9:39; Ac 8:4-7; Jas 2:5; Re 22:17 the poor. 13; 7:22,23; 1Sa 2:8; Ps 113:7,8; Mt 11:5,28 the halt. Ps 38:7; Isa 33:23; 35:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-22","title":"Luke 14:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>it is. Ac 1:1-9:43 and yet. Ps 103:6; 130:7; Joh 14:2; Eph 3:8; Col 2:9; 1Ti 2:5,6; 1Jo 2:2 Re 7:4-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-23","title":"Luke 14:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Go. Ps 98:3; Isa 11:10; 19:24,25; 27:13; 49:5,6; 66:19,20; Zec 14:8,9 Mal 1:11; Mt 21:43; 22:9,10; 28:19,20; Ac 9:15; 10:44-48; 11:18-21 Ac 13:47,48; 18:6; 22:21,22; 26:18-20; 28:28; Ro 10:18; 15:9-12 Eph 2:11-22; Col 1:23 compel. 24:29; Ge 19:2,3; Ps 110:3; Ac 16:15; Ro 11:13,14; 1Co 9:19-23 2Co 5:11,20; 6:1; Col 1:28; 2Ti 4:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-24","title":"Luke 14:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Pr 1:24-32; Mt 21:43; 22:8; 23:38,39; Joh 3:19,36; 8:21,24; Ac 13:46 Heb 12:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-25","title":"Luke 14:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>12:1; Joh 6:24-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-26","title":"Luke 14:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>any. De 13:6-8; 33:9; Ps 73:25,26; Mt 10:37; Php 3:8 hate. Ge 29:30,31; De 21:15; Job 7:15,16; Ec 2:17-19; Mal 1:2,3 Joh 12:25; Ro 9:13 yea. Ac 20:24; Re 12:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-27","title":"Luke 14:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>doth. 9:23-25; Mt 10:38; 16:24-26; Mr 8:34-37; 10:21; 15:21; Joh 19:17 2Ti 3:12 cannot. Mt 13:21; Ac 14:22; 2Ti 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-28","title":"Luke 14:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>intending. Ge 11:4-9; Pr 24:27 counteth. 33; Jos 24:19-24; Mt 8:20; 10:22; 20:22,23; Ac 21:13; 1Th 3:4,5 2Pe 1:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-30","title":"Luke 14:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Mt 7:27; 27:3-8; Ac 1:18,19; 1Co 3:11-14; Heb 6:4-8,11; 10:38 2Pe 2:19-22; 2Jo 1:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-31","title":"Luke 14:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>1Ki 20:11; 2Ki 18:20-22; Pr 20:18; 25:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-32","title":"Luke 14:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>and desireth. 12:58; 1Ki 20:31-34; 2Ki 10:4,5; Job 40:9; Mt 5:25; Ac 12:20 Jas 4:6-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-33","title":"Luke 14:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>26; 5:11,28; 18:22,23,28-30; Ac 5:1-5; 8:19-22; Php 3:7,8; 2Ti 4:10 1Jo 2:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-34","title":"Luke 14:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>Salt.Common salt, or muriate of soda, consists of soda in combination with muriatic acid, and is for the most part an artificial preparation from sea water, though found in some countries in a solid and massive state. See particularly Le 2:13.</p>\n<p>but. Mt 5:13; Mr 9:49,50; Col 4:6; Heb 2:4-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-14-35","title":"Luke 14:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>but. Joh 15:6 He. 8:8; 9:44; Mt 11:15; 13:9; Re 2:7,11,17,29</p>"}]}